---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ClathrusCaseStudy from '../../../components/ClathrusCaseStudy';
---
<Base title="The Case of the Wandering Devil's Fingers" description="A real fungal citizen-science investigation: trace what iNaturalist records revealed about Clathrus archeri in Ukraine, and learn what a range extension can and cannot establish.">
  <div class="mv-case-page">
    <section class="mv-case-hero">
      <div class="mv-case-hero-copy">
        <p class="mv-kicker">INVESTIGATE / REAL SCIENCE, RECREATED</p>
        <p class="mv-case-series">RESEARCH CASE STUDY 001 · DISTRIBUTION & BIODIVERSITY</p>
        <h1>The Case of the <em>Wandering Devil's Fingers</em></h1>
        <p>One unusual mushroom. An observation near Kyiv. A gap of roughly 350 kilometers in the previously documented record. But what did the researchers actually discover?</p>
        <a href="#investigation" class="mv-case-start">Follow the evidence ↓</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="mv-case-hero-photo">
        <img src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Clathrus_archeri_100906693.jpg" alt="Red finger-like fruiting arms of Clathrus archeri in a woodland setting" loading="eager" decoding="async"/>
        <figcaption>Illustrative photograph of <i>Clathrus archeri</i> (not a specimen from the Ukrainian study). © Matteo Marcandella, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clathrus_archeri_100906693.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY 4.0</a>.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="mv-case-overview">
      <span>HOW IT WORKS</span><p>Explore seven short chapters, make predictions, evaluate evidence, and compare your reasoning with the published study. No grades, no account, and no scientific conclusions invented by AI.</p>
      <p><strong>Source of truth:</strong> Prylutskyi & Kapets (2024), <i>State-of-the-Art of iNaturalist as a Source of Data on Ukrainian Fungi</i>, <i>Citizen Science: Theory and Practice</i>. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5334/cstp.717" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the original paper ↗</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="mv-case-workspace" id="investigation">
      <ClathrusCaseStudy client:load/>
    </section>
    <section class="mv-case-attribution">
      <p class="mv-kicker">RESEARCH TRANSPARENCY</p><h2>Learn from the researchers. Follow their sources.</h2>
      <p>This learning experience is an educational adaptation of one distribution example in a much broader published research paper. We are not claiming to have independently replicated the authors' analysis, verified the original observation, or established a current range boundary. Study snapshot: June 1, 2024. The paper is available under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY 4.0</a>; its original data and R analysis code are linked below.</p>
      <div class="mv-case-attribution-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.5334/cstp.717">Original article ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/olehprylutskyi/inaturalist_ua_paper">Authors' code and data ↗</a><a href="/investigate/study-designer/?framework=BIO-01&case=clathrus-archeri">Try the BIO-01 Research Navigator ↗</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
